  "hypothesis": "The run-provenance integrity claim -- content-addressable, append-only, Haber-Stornetta hash-chained run archive where any single-bit mutation of any artifact fails verify_run -- is reproducible by an independent implementation that shares no code with the Rust runtime, and that independent implementation reproduces the shipped canonical-JSON hash anchors bit-exact.",
  "module": "amphora-run-provenance",
  "non_circularity": "The oracle imports NO amphora Rust/Python runtime code; it re-implements canonicalize/stable_hash/RunArchive/verify_run from the primary literature and the published algorithm spec, then reproduces anchors the Rust runtime emitted (diagnostic_sha256 is stable_hash of a nested object, so matching it proves canonical-JSON parity, not mere file-copy).",
